WEBVTT

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:07.590
May 5th 11:40

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:10.010
Musashi, Time until Uraga Channel Arrival: 20 Min.

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:20.100
Ships Two, Three and Four are crippled.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.520
Ship One, travel speed, no more than six knots.

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:27.770
At this rate, the Musashi will enter
the Uraga Channel in 20 minutes!

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:37.080
<i>I repeat. All citizens, please evacuate
to the designated ships immediately.</i>

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:46.460
<i>Principal. We have a call from the Harekaze.</i>

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.090
<i>This is Misaki, captain of the Harekaze.</i>

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:52.590
<i>Please give us permission to execute
our plan against the Musashi.</i>

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:03.100
All of my classmates agree with the plan.

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:04.980
Please let us carry it out.

00:01:24.410 --> 00:01:26.120
I, Mayuki Munetani, principal of

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:31.000
<i>Yokosuka Girls' Marine High School, give you
permission to take action against the Musashi.</i>

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:34.010
<i>However, you may only attack once.</i>

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:37.010
<i>Ground forces are also preparing
to deal with the Musashi.</i>

00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:39.510
<i>There's no need for repetitive attacks.</i>

00:01:40.430 --> 00:01:44.520
<i>If you buy us five minutes...
no, three minutes, that should be plenty.</i>

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:45.520
Yes, ma'am.

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:47.850
Wait, Principal Munetani!

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:52.150
The Musashi has already disabled
three Blue Mermaid ships.

00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:54.030
The Harekaze by itself is too...

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:57.240
<i>The Musashi will enter the Uraga Channel
in 20 minutes.</i>

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:01.370
<i>Sis... I mean, Director Munetani.</i>

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:05.460
We may not be able to stop the Musashi.

00:02:06.410 --> 00:02:10.670
But, we will be able to buy you some time
by slowing it down.

00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:17.340
<i>Besides, Moka... I mean the captain of
the Musashi is under siege on the bridge.</i>

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:19.180
You can communicate with
the captain of the Musashi?

00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:25.520
We can't get through by radio, but we can
communicate with flashing light signals.

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:33.190
Captain Misaki, I acknowledge your plan
to approach the Musashi and take action against it.

00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:35.690
We're counting on you.

00:02:35.990 --> 00:02:36.860
Yes, ma'am.

00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:42.950
Let's go, Captain.

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:45.830
We're stronger when we're the hunters
instead of the prey!

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:48.460
- That's right.
- Aye, aye.

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:51.460
Captain, your orders.

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:55.210
30 degrees, steady as she goes!

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:57.090
30 degrees, steady as she goes!

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:58.840
Full speed ahead!

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:00.720
Full speed ahead!

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:24.240
<i>30 away from the Musashi.</i>

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:29.830
The Harekaze is approaching.

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:31.710
The Harekaze?

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:36.000
I sent them a signal to not get close.

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:38.170
Mike...

00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:42.010
- Tama, aim for the Musashi's main gun turret.
- Aye.

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:43.890
Let's stop the Musashi, no matter what.

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:46.010
Aye...

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:50.890
Mei, when we line up with the Musashi,
launch all our torpedoes.

00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:55.150
The coveted "launch of all torpedoes at once".
For real?!

00:03:55.360 --> 00:04:00.240
We'll probably only get one chance to fire.
I want to stop them with that one chance.

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:02.530
Let's aim at their stern.

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:06.490
Understood. I swear I'll hit the mark.

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:08.200
Ricchan, Kayo, let's go!

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:10.460
Yes, ma'am!

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:11.960
Roger!

00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:33.400
<i>Mike... Don't tell me.</i>

00:04:33.650 --> 00:04:36.520
Target is the Musashi's stern. Commence fire!

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:40.110
Our target is the Musashi's stern.
Let's have all torpedoes hit the target.

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:41.650
Prepare to fire!

00:04:41.650 --> 00:04:42.530
Fire!

00:04:53.420 --> 00:04:55.290
No good. We're not even making a dent.

00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:08.180
All right! 100% accuracy!

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:11.180
The Musashi is slowing down!

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:19.900
Here they come!

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:21.440
All personnel, brace for impact!

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:29.370
<i>The Musashi has fired!</i>

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:41.710
Are you all right?

00:05:42.550 --> 00:05:43.630
Thank you.

00:05:44.590 --> 00:05:45.590
Captain.

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:54.680
The Harekaze...

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:57.520
<i>Our stern smoke generator is disabled!</i>

00:05:57.520 --> 00:05:59.230
<i>The torpedo launcher is damaged!</i>

00:05:59.230 --> 00:06:01.190
<i>Fire in Number Five operation shed!</i>

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:02.780
Extinguishing the fire now!

00:06:04.610 --> 00:06:06.950
Th-They did so much damage
with just one attack.

00:06:07.410 --> 00:06:08.820
They really are powerful.

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:14.080
No good. It's broken.

00:06:14.450 --> 00:06:16.080
<i>The radio's broken.</i>

00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:17.920
The radio, too?

00:06:20.090 --> 00:06:22.090
Captain. We bought them five minutes.

00:06:22.670 --> 00:06:25.130
Rin, get us away from the Musashi.

00:06:25.130 --> 00:06:26.510
Leave it to me!

00:06:36.020 --> 00:06:37.350
The Musashi fired!

00:06:38.310 --> 00:06:39.230
Here they come!

00:06:49.070 --> 00:06:50.030
Mike!

00:06:54.290 --> 00:06:56.330
<i>Number One firing system is disabled!</i>

00:06:56.330 --> 00:06:59.830
<i>Fire in the dining hall!
Going in now to extinguish it!</i>

00:07:00.170 --> 00:07:01.790
This is the Musashi?

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:03.840
It's keeping us from moving ahead!

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:05.590
There's nowhere to run!

00:07:09.970 --> 00:07:10.890
Captain?

00:07:10.890 --> 00:07:12.100
What's wrong?

00:07:12.470 --> 00:07:13.810
I'm going to stop the bombarding.

00:07:13.810 --> 00:07:14.600
That's absurd!

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:15.720
Captain!

00:07:16.980 --> 00:07:19.020
If I don't, the Harekaze will...

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:23.110
Please calm down, Captain.

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:28.030
I'm sorry.

00:07:33.990 --> 00:07:36.200
Chief Engineer! Water! Water!

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:38.000
What? I'm on my way!

00:07:38.330 --> 00:07:40.750
<i>Captain, our port side engine room is flooding!</i>

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:45.880
Get all the pumps in here!
Don't let the furnace go out!

00:07:46.380 --> 00:07:47.840
Even the engine room...

00:07:51.550 --> 00:07:54.390
Captain, shall I have everyone
prepare to evacuate?

00:07:54.550 --> 00:07:56.010
For real? We're going to run away?

00:07:56.350 --> 00:08:00.310
If a snake's head gets eaten,
it can't revive itself anymore.

00:08:00.310 --> 00:08:04.110
I'm sorry! If I were better at maneuvering...

00:08:07.690 --> 00:08:09.030
Aye...

00:08:11.910 --> 00:08:12.860
Everyone...

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:22.120
All personnel! Prepare to evac—

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:30.880
What's this?

00:08:31.220 --> 00:08:32.800
Rin, hard right rudder!

00:08:33.090 --> 00:08:34.510
Hard right rudder.

00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:41.600
<i>Visual confirmation of ships behind us!</i>

00:08:41.980 --> 00:08:43.480
Is it the Blue Mermaids?

00:08:43.480 --> 00:08:44.480
I'll go look!

00:08:53.240 --> 00:08:55.070
Identification signals confirmed.

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:56.120
The Hiei,

00:08:56.570 --> 00:08:57.450
the Maikaze,

00:08:57.830 --> 00:08:58.740
the Hamakaze,

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:00.290
the Admiral Spee,

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:03.370
and then, it's the Tenjin!

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:08.000
The Tenjin?

00:09:08.380 --> 00:09:10.010
It's our school's ships!

00:09:21.020 --> 00:09:27.020
Episode 12: In a Pinch with the Last Battle!

00:09:31.570 --> 00:09:32.780
Instructor Furushou!

00:09:33.110 --> 00:09:36.660
I'm glad we made it in time,
but I'm sorry we're late.

00:09:37.530 --> 00:09:40.790
Ms. Noma, let them know
we can't use our radio.

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:46.290
Coco! Everyone!

00:09:46.710 --> 00:09:49.670
You came for us!

00:09:53.550 --> 00:09:56.180
The time to pay back our debt has come!

00:09:58.260 --> 00:09:59.680
Captain, what should we do?

00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:03.180
With everyone else here, we can keep fighting!

00:10:05.190 --> 00:10:06.940
I have no objections.

00:10:08.230 --> 00:10:11.190
Change of plan.
We're going to board the Musashi!

00:10:11.190 --> 00:10:12.820
- All right!
- Aye!

00:10:12.820 --> 00:10:14.490
- I'll do my best!
- Yes!

00:10:14.490 --> 00:10:16.490
- Let's do this!
- Let's do it!

00:10:16.490 --> 00:10:18.700
<i>The Spee is asking what the plan is.</i>

00:10:19.910 --> 00:10:22.660
We're going to board the Musashi.
Please support the Harekaze!

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:29.420
"Please... give... us... support."

00:10:29.670 --> 00:10:31.540
That's what they said, Captain.

00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:35.300
Roger that. Leave it to us.

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:50.310
We're going to support the Harekaze
and their plan to board the Musashi.

00:10:50.810 --> 00:10:53.780
The Tenjin and the Spee will attack
the Musashi's starboard side,

00:10:53.780 --> 00:10:59.030
and the Hiei, the Maikaze, and Hamakaze will
attack from the port side to provide covering fire.

00:10:59.030 --> 00:11:01.490
All ships, prepare to attack.

00:11:02.280 --> 00:11:04.240
Your target is the Musashi!

00:11:06.370 --> 00:11:09.580
The wind is blowing. The wind of hope.

00:11:10.290 --> 00:11:12.090
All ships, attack!

00:11:33.900 --> 00:11:34.690
Do not falter!

00:11:59.130 --> 00:12:02.890
Remind all of the ships not to hit
anywhere near the Musashi's bridge.

00:12:02.890 --> 00:12:03.800
Understood.

00:12:04.140 --> 00:12:05.140
And the Harekaze?

00:12:15.230 --> 00:12:16.980
We need to get in there somehow.

00:12:17.400 --> 00:12:21.150
Captain. Could this be of any use?

00:12:22.780 --> 00:12:23.870
A Type 4 rocket?

00:12:24.410 --> 00:12:27.870
The Akashi crew thought it might
come in handy, so they equipped us.

00:12:29.660 --> 00:12:31.000
Tama! Mei!

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:32.000
Aye?

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:37.960
All right, got it!

00:12:37.960 --> 00:12:38.840
Aye!

00:12:39.010 --> 00:12:39.630
Rin!

00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:40.720
Yes, ma'am?!

00:12:41.010 --> 00:12:43.220
Please get us in front of the Musashi.

00:12:43.390 --> 00:12:45.800
I-I-In front of the bow?!

00:12:45.800 --> 00:12:47.010
Ms. Shiretoko.

00:12:49.770 --> 00:12:51.640
Full speed, to the front of the Musashi!

00:12:52.190 --> 00:12:53.900
S-Steady as she goes!

00:12:58.690 --> 00:13:00.530
They're going to cut in front of the Musashi?

00:13:00.530 --> 00:13:04.410
Don't let them hit the Harekaze.
Draw the Musashi's fire over here!

00:13:05.570 --> 00:13:06.660
Fire!

00:13:12.460 --> 00:13:14.500
Go, Harekaze.

00:13:23.170 --> 00:13:26.140
- Tama, there's no time, so let's hurry.
- Aye.

00:13:36.940 --> 00:13:39.270
The rocket is ready to go anytime!

00:13:39.570 --> 00:13:43.780
Full speed ahead! Hard right rudder!
Get our stern facing the Musashi!

00:13:44.110 --> 00:13:47.200
Full speed ahead! Hard right rudder!

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:53.330
Tama, prepare to fire!

00:13:56.670 --> 00:13:58.920
Tama, fire with your soul!

00:14:04.670 --> 00:14:08.050
With this shot, we'll grab our chance!

00:14:27.610 --> 00:14:29.530
- Captain! Now!
- Aye!

00:14:30.200 --> 00:14:33.290
Rin, hard right rudder!
To the Musashi's starboard side!

00:14:33.620 --> 00:14:35.160
Hard right rudder!

00:14:45.050 --> 00:14:47.430
T-The wheel won't turn!

00:14:47.630 --> 00:14:48.130
What?

00:14:48.130 --> 00:14:51.300
<i>Captain, the rudder was hit!
Steering is disabled!</i>

00:14:54.850 --> 00:14:56.390
We have a parachute, right?

00:14:56.810 --> 00:14:57.690
Y-Yeah!

00:14:58.270 --> 00:15:00.440
Hime, Momo, prepare the parachute!

00:15:02.270 --> 00:15:05.320
The parachute is tied on, but now what?

00:15:05.650 --> 00:15:07.450
Throw it to rear starboard!

00:15:08.570 --> 00:15:10.370
- Hurry!
- Yes ma'am!

00:15:26.420 --> 00:15:27.300
We turned!

00:15:27.300 --> 00:15:29.590
We did it! We're facing the enemy!

00:15:29.930 --> 00:15:32.720
I don't care what happens to the tin can!
Don't you stop!

00:15:33.970 --> 00:15:35.100
I see the Musashi!

00:15:35.220 --> 00:15:36.640
Cut the parachute loose!

00:15:43.610 --> 00:15:45.150
- We're going to crash into it!
- Brace yourselves!

00:16:09.300 --> 00:16:12.300
We did it! The attack was a success!

00:16:12.300 --> 00:16:13.890
Rescue team, prepare to board!

00:16:13.890 --> 00:16:15.180
<i>We're ready.</i>

00:16:15.810 --> 00:16:18.810
Here we go! Storm the ship!

00:16:23.310 --> 00:16:24.190
Captain.

00:16:25.360 --> 00:16:27.190
Go ahead and board the ship too, Captain.

00:16:28.360 --> 00:16:30.900
I-I'll stay here.

00:16:30.900 --> 00:16:32.160
I'm the captain.

00:16:32.610 --> 00:16:34.450
Go, Ms. Misaki.

00:16:37.490 --> 00:16:39.120
I know how you feel.

00:16:40.080 --> 00:16:42.460
You have "I want to go"
written all over your face.

00:16:44.330 --> 00:16:45.960
Shiro...

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:47.710
Thank you!

00:16:52.340 --> 00:16:55.760
That's my friend, all right. You're so cool, Shiro!

00:16:55.760 --> 00:16:57.970
No, we're not friends.

00:17:03.230 --> 00:17:04.730
Moka!

00:17:11.400 --> 00:17:12.360
<i>Moka!</i>

00:17:20.580 --> 00:17:22.250
Moka!

00:17:27.380 --> 00:17:28.750
Moka!

00:17:30.420 --> 00:17:31.210
Mike!

00:17:52.490 --> 00:17:55.360
We finally see each other again, Mike.

00:17:57.030 --> 00:17:58.780
Moka.

00:18:00.290 --> 00:18:01.580
Moka.

00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:03.790
Moka.

00:18:04.460 --> 00:18:06.460
Moka!

00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:12.420
Mike, you're so reckless.

00:18:12.420 --> 00:18:13.550
Because...

00:18:13.550 --> 00:18:15.090
You're really something.

00:18:15.090 --> 00:18:16.340
I'm sorry.

00:18:16.970 --> 00:18:19.430
But, thank you.

00:18:20.890 --> 00:18:24.270
<i>The operation is over.
All ships, return to Yokosuka Harbor!</i>

00:18:29.270 --> 00:18:32.650
Mom, you missed your chance
to create a legend.

00:18:33.490 --> 00:18:35.150
In my stead...

00:18:35.950 --> 00:18:39.280
...my students did it for me.

00:20:07.790 --> 00:20:09.250
We're home.

00:20:11.460 --> 00:20:13.670
Ground!

00:20:14.250 --> 00:20:15.920
We made it back home.

00:20:15.920 --> 00:20:18.260
I still can't believe it.

00:20:18.720 --> 00:20:20.430
It's not a dream!

00:20:20.430 --> 00:20:21.260
Aye.

00:20:34.440 --> 00:20:35.440
What's wrong?

00:20:35.440 --> 00:20:36.440
No way.

00:20:37.150 --> 00:20:37.980
Oh no...

00:20:38.490 --> 00:20:39.900
The Harekaze...

00:20:41.110 --> 00:20:42.660
Somebody stop it.

00:20:42.820 --> 00:20:44.780
Don't sink!

00:20:44.950 --> 00:20:46.080
No!

00:20:46.080 --> 00:20:47.330
Harekaze!
